            <section>
               <title value="Hospital course note"/>
               <code>
                  <coding>
                     <system value="http://loinc.org"/>
                     <code value="8648-8"/>
                     <display value="Hospital course note"/>
                  </coding>
               </code>
               <text>
                  <status value="generated"/>
                  <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">Dear colleague, I am writing to inform you about the hospital course of your patient, a 69-year-old male admitted on 02/01/2013 due to an acute exacerbation of his known chronic obstructive pulmonary disease. On admission, he presented with increased dyspnoea, productive cough, and reduced oxygen saturation. Diagnostic workup included chest X-ray confirming hyperinflation without consolidation, arterial blood gas analysis revealing hypoxaemia with mild hypercapnia, and pulse oximetry monitoring throughout the stay. Blood tests showed mild inflammatory markers. Treatment consisted of controlled oxygen therapy, nebulised bronchodilators (salbutamol and ipratropium), systemic corticosteroids, and intravenous fluid support. The patient responded well to treatment with significant symptomatic improvement. He was discharged on 03/01/2013 in stable condition. We recommend continuation of optimised inhaler therapy and close outpatient follow-up. Please do not hesitate to contact me for further information.</div>
               </text>
            </section>
